{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"tardy-dependable-dinosaur","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# Jira DC hardening — follow-on to e369\n\n## Context\n\nEpic [rebar:e369-a449-4773-48fb] delivered Jira Server/Data Center support and met its\noperator-approved exit bar: the live DC harness green end to end (run **30964805133**: 62 passed,\n1 xfailed, 0 failed, canary `collected=63 executed=62 skipped=1`), 58 descendants, 0 uncertified.\n\nThis epic holds the DC work discovered BY that delivery which is hardening rather than the feature\nitself. It exists so no DC bug is left unparented while e369 closes on the scope it actually shipped.\nOperator decision, 2026-08-05: allow e369 to close; continue hardening here.\n\n## What is in scope\n\n* [rebar:4a6d-5bbc-44f4-4a56] (bug) — the THIRD live-DC channel never got 9790's readiness rule.\n  `.github/workflows/jira-dc-capability-map.yml` gates on the same cheap `serverInfo` curl loop, then\n  runs the mapper whose job is to record the Epic-field ids as the DECLARED CONTRACT a human commits.\n  Worse than the two channels already fixed, because it **reports rather than fails**: a fast run\n  silently writes a WRONG contract instead of erroring.\n* [rebar:a3fa-...] (bug) — capability call sites are cast but not runtime-guarded, so a non-capable\n  transport fails silently.\n* [rebar:f020-0960-2c42-4d61] (task) — decide the fate of the dormant absence-probe port\n  (`probe_remote` / `SupportsAbsenceProbe` / `inbound_probe.py`) left dormant by 3b5f. **Blocked on an\n  operator decision**, not on engineering: deleting it removes DC's only import of the shared\n  `classify_probe_response`, which weakens e369 AC5's both-backends claim.\n\n## Explicitly NOT in scope\n\nCloud-surface defects found by DC parity guards ([rebar:6194-...], [rebar:6a74-...],\n[rebar:9a46-...]) — real, but Cloud's, not DC feature delivery. The general vacuous-guard class\n([rebar:8a5e-b88e-0c3e-4544]) and capability-map trust infrastructure\n([rebar:a9bd-6641-e603-42bc]) are tracked on their own tickets; a9bd was explicitly unparented by\noperator instruction.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] 4a6d is fixed: the capability-map workflow waits on the same shared field-readiness definition\n      `scripts/jira_dc_field_readiness.py` that the harness and the probe now delegate to, so all\n      THREE live-DC channels share one definition and cannot drift\n- [ ] the map run FAILS rather than reports when the contract cannot be established — proven by a test\n      that pins a system-only inventory as not-ready on that surface, not merely by configuration\n- [ ] a3fa is fixed: capability casts are runtime-guarded so a non-capable transport fails loudly\n      rather than silently, with a test that pins the loud failure\n- [ ] f020 is decided and the decision recorded with its reason, including what it does to e369 AC5's\n      both-backends claim on `classify_probe_response`\n- [ ] the live DC harness is still GREEN end to end after this epic's changes (0 failed cells) —\n      inherited from e369's exit bar, so hardening cannot regress the delivered feature\n- [ ] no cell is deleted, skipped or `xfail`ed to reach green (the standing operator constraint)\n\n## Testing\n\n    gh workflow run \"Live External Integration\" --ref main    # the live DC harness\n    pytest -m \"not integration and not external\" -n 4 --dist worksteal -q\n    make lint && make typecheck","id":"5796-d1f8-870f-4dc1","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"epic","title":"Jira DC hardening — follow-on to e369 (readiness parity, capability guards, dormant port)"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785904271395690001,"uuid":"c0fcdf99-7f52-4a4c-a413-cd4f4882898a"}